## ArrayList.Clear()

The contract test for the ArrayList.Clear() method looks like this:
```csharp
[PexMethod]
[PexExploration]
public void ClearContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList) {
    ArrayList Old_arrList = (ArrayList) arrList.Clone();

    arrList.Clear();

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;

    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList", Old_arrList);
    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", New_arrListCount);

    Assert.AreEqual(0, New_arrListCount);
    Assert.IsTrue(arrList.TrueForAll(x => x == null));
}
```

The contract test for the ArrayList.TrimToSize() method is shown in the previous section. This method trims the capacity of the ArrayList to be the actual number of elements, which may reduce the size of the ArrayList if it is larger than necessary for storing its elements.

The contracts for the Clear and TrimToSize methods assume the state of the ArrayList is unchanged except for the Count property, which must be zero after invocation of these methods. It also checks that all elements in the ArrayList are null. It might be necessary to add other specific conditions depending on the expected behavior of the specific ArrayList implementation.

## ArrayList.CopyTo()

The CopyTo method of ArrayList copies the entire ArrayList to a compatible one-dimensional array, starting at the specified index of the target array. The contract test for the CopyTo() method looks like this:
```csharp
[PexMethod]
[PexExploration]
public void CopyToContract([PexAssumeUnderTest] ArrayList arrList, [PexArrayOf]object objArr, int index) {

    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(arrList.Count <= objArr.Length - index);

    ArrayList Old_arrList = (ArrayList) arrList.Clone();

    arrList.CopyTo(objArr, index);

    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList", Old_arrList);
    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_objArr", objArr);

    if (arrList.Count > 0) {
        Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrList[0], objArr[index]);
    }
}
```

This contract test assumes that the source array is large enough to accommodate the items in the list at the specified index. It also checks that the first item in the ArrayList matches the item at the specified index in the copy array after the CopyTo method call.

